  "result": "I fixed it. Completion was cutting off any argument at a `#`.\n\n**Cause:** `split_arg_string` in `src/click/shell_completion.py` uses `shlex.shlex` to split up the command line, and `shlex` treats `#` as the start of a comment by default. So `cli --opt a#b` was read as `[\"cli\", \"--opt\", \"a\"]`, and `cli #b` lost `#b` completely. The command line Click gets has already been processed by the shell, so `#` there is just a normal character. This affected bash, zsh, fish and PowerShell, since they all use this function.\n\n**Fix:** I added one line, `lex.commenters = \"\"`, right after `lex.whitespace_split = True` (`src/click/shell_completion.py:625`), so `#` is no longer treated as a comment.\n\n**Tests:** I added three cases to `test_split_arg_string` in `tests/test_parser.py`: `cli a#b`, `cli #b` and `cli 'a #b'`. Without the fix, the first two fail; with it, all pass. The quoted case passed either way. The full test suite passes (1909 passed, 102 skipped, 1 xfailed).\n\nI didn't add a `CHANGES.md` entry because the newest section there (8.5.0) is already released. Tell me which version to file it under and I'll add one. Nothing is committed yet.",
